{
  "run_id": "PMC12985727__expert_context__web_trend_focus_ground_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The initial TiVNbTa alloy has a single-phase BCC dendritic microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiVNbTa is used as an intermediate layer between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add 1–5 at.% Mo to TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cyclic tensile and compressive loading near 1273 K mimics the operational environment of plasma-facing divertor components.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After Mo addition, the alloy will retain a homogeneous single-phase BCC lattice with Mo incorporated into the matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo atoms incorporated into the matrix will act as obstacles to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will stabilize the microstructure against coarsening and deleterious phase changes.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo provides solid-solution strengthening in related refractory HEAs.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, Mo will impede dislocation mobility, particularly behavior associated with the transition from screw to edge dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed dislocation mechanism will enhance plateau strength and retard high-temperature yield-strength degradation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::024::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo strengthening will occur without compromising ductility or heat-transfer performance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, adding Mo will increase TiVNbTa yield strength from approximately 330 MPa to at least 450 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, adding Mo will improve the compressive strength of TiVNbTa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5978046::web::011::4_conclusions",
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-modified alloy will retain ductility near 40% strain at 1273 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-modified alloy will preserve the thermal conductivity required for efficient heat transfer between W and CuCrZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped TiVNbTa has approximately 330 MPa yield strength, 423 MPa compressive strength, and around 40% ductility at 1273 K.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
